{{!--
  The template packaging/rust-licenses.sh fills in with cargo-about to make
  packaging/THIRD-PARTY-rust.txt. Plain text, so every value is in triple
  braces: double ones would escape <, > and & for HTML, and the e-mail
  addresses in crates' authors with them. Patina itself is in what
  cargo-about gathers and is left out here; its LICENSE goes beside this file
  in every package. The Slint section has to stay last: the script adds the
  licence's text after it.
--}}
Rust crates compiled into Patina
================================

Generated from Cargo.lock by packaging/rust-licenses.sh in Patina's
repository, with cargo-about; not to be edited by hand.

patina, the program, is built from the Rust crates listed below. The same
list serves every package, though each platform compiles only some of them.
Each crate is under its own licence or licences, named beside it as the
crate states them. Where a crate offers a choice, Patina passes it on under
the one its entry appears under in "Licence texts", where the text follows,
in the crate's own copy wherever it ships one. Each crate's source is in its
repository, given beside it, and on crates.io at that version. The rest of
the software in Patina's packages is listed in THIRD-PARTY.md.

